<%# locals: (faqs:) -%>
<% picks = [
  [ "keystone", "Best all-around for young kids", "Kidtopia family activities, a gondola from River Run Village, lots of gentle terrain, and about a 90-minute drive from Denver without traffic." ],
  [ "beaver-creek", "Best for an easy, polished trip", "A car-free village with outdoor escalators and an ice rink, quiet slopes, and free warm cookies at the base every afternoon. Fly into Eagle (EGE) to skip most of I-70." ],
  [ "aspen-snowmass", "Best for mixed-ability families", "Snowmass is the biggest of the four Aspen mountains, with long cruisers, ski-in/ski-out lodging, and the Treehouse kids' center at the base." ],
  [ "steamboat", "Best for a ski trip that skips I-70", "Direct winter flights into Yampa Valley (HDN), wide intermediate runs, a real ranch town, and hot springs for tired legs." ],
  [ "copper-mountain", "Best for families who ski at different levels", "Copper's terrain is naturally divided: easier runs to the west, harder to the east, so everyone can find their level and meet up at the base." ],
  [ "winter-park", "Best for a drive from Denver", "One of the closest big resorts to Denver, dedicated beginner terrain, and lodging in town with free shuttles. The Winter Park Express ski train has run from Denver Union Station on select dates." ],
  [ "breckenridge", "Best for a lively town", "A walkable historic main street, ski school at both base areas, and lots to do off the slopes. Base elevation is high (9,600 ft), so take the first day easy." ]
] %>
<% budget = [
  [ "loveland", "About an hour from Denver with lower ticket prices and no village to pay for. Great for day trips from the Front Range." ],
  [ "eldora", "The closest ski area to Boulder, with a compact layout that's easy to manage with kids." ],
  [ "ski-cooper", "A small, affordable hill near Leadville with mostly easy and intermediate terrain." ],
  [ "monarch-mountain", "A no-frills local favorite with natural snow and short lift lines." ],
  [ "purgatory", "Southwest Colorado near Durango, known for friendly beginner and intermediate terrain." ]
] %>
<% resorts = Resort.where(slug: (picks + budget).map(&:first)).index_by(&:slug) %>
<div class="tldr"><p><strong>Short answer:</strong> the best Colorado ski resorts for families are Keystone for young kids, Beaver Creek for an easy, polished trip, Snowmass for mixed-ability groups, Steamboat to skip I-70 traffic, and Copper, Winter Park and Breckenridge for drive-in trips from Denver. On a budget, Loveland, Eldora and Ski Cooper are smaller, cheaper and easy to manage with kids.</p></div>

<h2>Best Colorado ski resorts for families</h2>
<ol>
  <% picks.each do |slug, label, why| %>
    <% r = resorts[slug] or next %>
    <li><strong><%= link_to r.name, resort_path(r) %>: <%= label.downcase_first %>.</strong> <%= why %><% if Lodging.slugs.include?(slug) %> See <%= link_to "where to stay in #{r.name}", where_to_stay_resort_path(r) %>.<% end %></li>
  <% end %>
</ol>

<h2>Colorado family resorts compared</h2>
<table>
  <caption>Colorado family ski resorts: pass, airport, base elevation, and vertical drop</caption>
  <thead><tr><th scope="col">Resort</th><th scope="col">Pass</th><th scope="col">Fly into</th><th scope="col">Base elevation</th><th scope="col">Vertical</th></tr></thead>
  <tbody>
    <% picks.each do |slug, _, _| %>
      <% r = resorts[slug] or next %>
      <tr><th scope="row"><%= link_to r.name, resort_path(r) %></th><td><%= r.pass_label %></td><td><%= r.nearest_airport_code %></td><td><%= number_with_delimiter(r.elevation_base) %> ft</td><td><%= r.vertical_drop ? "#{number_with_delimiter(r.vertical_drop)} ft" : "–" %></td></tr>
    <% end %>
  </tbody>
</table>
<p>Pass coverage is for the 2026-27 season. Check <%= link_to "Ikon vs Epic", ikon_vs_epic_path %> for blackout dates and kids' pass options.</p>

<h2>Smaller, cheaper Colorado ski areas for families</h2>
<ul>
  <% budget.each do |slug, why| %>
    <% r = resorts[slug] or next %>
    <li><strong><%= link_to r.name, resort_path(r) %>:</strong> <%= why %></li>
  <% end %>
</ul>

<h2>Colorado tips for families</h2>
<h3>Plan around I-70</h3>
<p>Weekend and holiday traffic on I-70 between Denver and the mountains can turn a 90-minute drive into three hours or more. Travel midweek, leave early, or stay in the mountains. Flying into Eagle (EGE), Aspen (ASE), Hayden (HDN) or Gunnison (GUC) skips the drive for Vail, Beaver Creek, Aspen, Steamboat and Crested Butte.</p>
<h3>Take altitude seriously</h3>
<p>Most Colorado bases sit between 8,000 and 10,800 ft. Kids and adults coming from sea level can get headaches and feel tired. Drink plenty of water, keep the first day short, and sleep lower if you can.</p>
<h3>Book ski school early</h3>
<p>Kids' ski school sells out over Christmas, Presidents' Day and spring break. Book lessons when you book lodging, and stay close to the ski school drop-off.</p>
<h3>Pick your month</h3>
<p>For the deepest snow, most Colorado resorts peak from late December through March. Each resort's "best time to ski" page shows its snowiest months, for example <%= link_to "best time to ski Keystone", best_time_resort_path("keystone") %>. The <%= link_to "Colorado snow report", region_path("colorado") %> ranks every resort on this week's forecast.</p>

<h2>Next steps</h2>
<p>Read <%= link_to "how to choose a family ski resort", guide_path("best-family-ski-resorts") %> and <%= link_to "skiing with kids by age", guide_path("skiing-with-kids") %>, check <%= link_to "kids' ski gear and sizing", guide_path("kids-ski-gear") %>, then use the free <%= link_to "Ski Trip Planner", ski_trip_planner_path %> to plan the timeline and budget.</p>
<% faqs << { question: "What is the best ski resort in Colorado for families?", answer: "Keystone is a top pick for families with young kids thanks to its Kidtopia activities, gentle terrain and short drive from Denver. Beaver Creek, Snowmass, Steamboat, Copper, Winter Park and Breckenridge are also strong family choices, each for different reasons." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "Which Colorado ski resort is best for beginners and kids?", answer: "Keystone, Snowmass, Winter Park and Copper Mountain all have large beginner areas and strong kids' ski schools. Smaller areas like Loveland, Eldora and Ski Cooper are cheaper and easier to navigate for a first day." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "Which Colorado ski resort is closest to Denver for a family day trip?", answer: "Loveland, Eldora and Winter Park are among the closest ski areas to Denver and Boulder, roughly an hour to 90 minutes away without traffic. Summit County resorts like Keystone, Breckenridge and Copper are about 90 minutes to 2 hours." } %>
<% faqs << { question: "How do families avoid I-70 ski traffic in Colorado?", answer: "Drive midweek, leave before 7am on weekends, stay in the mountains instead of driving from Denver each day, or fly into a mountain airport like Eagle (EGE), Hayden (HDN) or Aspen (ASE)." } %>
